From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] AlarmManager: listener alarms keep their uid when the wake lock
 is handed on

When an alarm finished and another was still in flight, AlarmManagerService
attributed its wake lock to the next one with knownUid -1. For an alarm set
with a listener (no PendingIntent) setWakelockWorkSource() then called
getTarget() on a null PendingIntent; the NullPointerException was caught and
the wake lock charged to the system instead of the app. Found from a
system_server fault in the kernel log, mapped with oatdump to dex pc 0x44 of
setWakelockWorkSource (PW3 Android, Test V47); Wi-Fi's own alarms are listener
alarms, so it came with Wi-Fi state changes.

The first delivery already passes the alarm's uid for listener alarms
(deliverLocked); the hand-on now does the same.

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/AlarmManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/AlarmManagerService.java
@@ -3033,7 +3033,8 @@
                 if (mInFlight.size() > 0) {
                     InFlight inFlight = mInFlight.get(0);
                     setWakelockWorkSource(inFlight.mPendingIntent, inFlight.mWorkSource,
-                            inFlight.mAlarmType, inFlight.mTag, -1, false);
+                            inFlight.mAlarmType, inFlight.mTag,
+                            (inFlight.mPendingIntent == null) ? inFlight.mUid : -1, false);
                 } else {
                     // should never happen
                     mLog.w("Alarm wakelock still held but sent queue empty");
